hadiths[17]{hadithnumber,text}:
"891","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever frees a Muslim slave, Allah will free every limb of his in exchange for every limb of the slave from Hell, even his private part in exchange for the slave’s private part."
"892","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A son cannot fulfill the right of his father except in the case that he finds his father as a slave of someone, then buys him and sets him free."
"893","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Whoever frees his share in a slave, and he has enough wealth to pay the just value of the slave and give the shares of the other partners, then the slave will be free for him. (If he does not have enough wealth,) then only his own share will be free."
"894","`Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that` he (peace be upon him) said: Whoever frees his share in a slave, the freeing (i.e., the freeing of the remaining share) will also be from his wealth if he is wealthy. If he is not wealthy, then the slave should work and earn, and he should not be forced."
"895","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Imran bin Husain (may Allah be pleased with him) that a man, at the time of his death, freed his six slaves and he had no wealth other than them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) called for them and divided them into three groups. Then he drew lots and freed two of them, and kept the remaining four in slavery. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) spoke harshly regarding the deceased."
"896","‘Mother of the Believers, Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that Barirah came to me and said, “My masters have agreed to contract me for nine uqiyah, one uqiyah per year. So help me.” I said, “If your masters are willing, I will pay the whole amount at once and set you free, but the right of wala’ (allegiance) will be mine.” Lady Barirah (may Allah be pleased with her) mentioned this to her masters, but they refused and said, “The wala’ will be ours.” Then Barirah came to me and told me this, so I scolded her. She said, “By Allah, this will not happen.” Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) heard about this and asked me, so when I explained the whole situation, he said, “Buy her and set her free, and let the condition of wala’ be for them, for the wala’ is for the one who sets free.” So I did so. After that, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) gave a sermon in the evening, praised Allah as He deserves, and then said, “What is the matter with people who stipulate conditions that are not in the Book of Allah? Any condition that is not in the Book of Allah is invalid, even if it is stipulated a hundred times. The Book of Allah is more deserving, and Allah’s condition is stronger. Some of you say to others, ‘Set (the slave or slave-girl) free and the wala’ will be ours,’ even though the wala’ is only for the one who sets free.”"
"897","Narrated from Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that she said: Three things became known because of Barirah. One is that she was given the choice regarding her husband’s case when she was freed. The second is that she received (charity) meat. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came to me and there was meat cooking in a pot over the fire. He (peace be upon him) asked for food, so bread and some household curry were brought before him. He (peace be upon him) said: Wasn’t there meat cooking in the pot on the stove? The people said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah! But that meat was charity which was given to Barirah, and we thought it inappropriate to serve it to you. So he (peace be upon him) said: It was charity for her, but for us it is a gift from her side. The third is that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said regarding Barirah: Wala’ (the right of inheritance/loyalty) will belong to the one who sets free."
"898","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade the sale and gift of wala’."
"899","`Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that` he (peace be upon him) said: Whoever makes someone his mawla (protector or client) without the permission of his masters, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people, and on the Day of Resurrection, neither his obligatory nor his voluntary deeds will be accepted."
"900","Sayyiduna Abu Mas'ud Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I was beating my slave when suddenly I heard a voice from behind, saying, ""Abu Mas'ud! Know that indeed Allah has more power over you than you have over this slave."" I turned around and saw that it was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). I said, ""O Messenger of Allah! I have set him free for the sake of Allah (i.e., without any price or condition)."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""If you had not done so, the fire of Hell would have burned you or touched you."
"901","It is narrated from Zadhan that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) called one of his slaves and saw a mark on his back, so he asked, ""Did I cause you pain?"" He replied, ""No."" Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) said, ""You are free."" Then he picked something up from the ground and said, ""I did not even receive as much reward as this for freeing him. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: Whoever inflicts a legal punishment on his slave without a reason (i.e., beats him unjustly) or slaps him, its expiation (i.e., compensation, penalty) is that he should set him free."
"902","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Suwaid bin Muqarrin (may Allah be pleased with him) that when a man slapped his slave-girl, Sayyiduna Suwaid (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""Do you not know that hitting the face is forbidden? And look at me: in the blessed time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), we seven brothers had only one servant. One of my brothers slapped her, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered her to be set free."
"903","`Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that` Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever accuses his male or female slave of adultery, the punishment of false accusation (qadhf) will be imposed on him on the Day of Resurrection, except if he is truthful (then he will not be punished)."
"904","Ma’rur bin Suwaid says: We went to Abu Dharr Ghifari (may Allah be pleased with him) at (the place) Rabadhah. He was wearing a cloak, and his servant was also wearing a similar cloak. So we said, “O Abu Dharr! If you took both these cloaks, it would make a (proper) garment.” He said: There was a quarrel between me and one of my brothers. His mother was a non-Arab, so I insulted him by mentioning his mother. He complained about me to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). When I met the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), he said, “O Abu Dharr! You still have some traces of ignorance (i.e., the influence of the pre-Islamic era when people used to take pride in their parents and looked down upon the parents of others).” I said, “O Messenger of Allah! Whoever insults people, they will insult his parents.” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “O Abu Dharr! You still have some traces of ignorance (i.e., if he insulted you, the recompense was that you insult him back, not his parents). They are your brothers (from this it is understood that he was a servant, but Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) called him a brother because the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) also called them brothers). Allah Almighty has placed them under your authority (i.e., in your possession). Feed them what you eat yourself, and clothe them with what you wear yourself, and do not burden them beyond their capacity. If you assign them a task, then help them with it.”"
"905","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: When a servant prepares food for one of you, then brings it to him after having endured its heat and smoke, let him make him sit with him and eat, and if the food is little, then give him a morsel or two in his hand."
"906","Narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed, when a slave is sincere to his master and worships Allah well, then he will have a double or twofold reward (compared to a free person)."
"907","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A righteous slave will have a double reward (one for being loyal to his master and the other for worshipping Allah). By Him in Whose hand is the life of Abu Huraira, if it were not for jihad, Hajj, and good conduct towards my mother, I would have wished to die as a slave. And Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him), due to his companionship with and service to his mother, did not perform any (supererogatory) Hajj until she passed away."
